# `todo/t1373` / `todo/t1319`, STRING PAYLOAD — RECEIVER PLACE: STRUCT FIELD.
#
# The `Box[int]` sibling of this cell prints a pointer-shaped integer pre-fix.
# With a `String` payload the same wrong pointer is handed to the string
# printer, so the program emits raw heap bytes instead.
#
# RED-VERIFIED AS WRITTEN against the pre-fix compiler on C: prints garbage
# bytes at rc 0. POST-fix: `hi`.
#
# ⚠ ONE RECEIVER PLACE PER FILE — `ensure_extern` synthesizes ONE declaration
# per MANGLED SYMBOL from whichever call site is lowered FIRST, so a file with
# several places claims several cells in its NAME and pins one.
#
# ⛔ C-LANE-ONLY, BY DECLARATION AND NOT BY ACCIDENT. Its test opens with
# `skip_under_llvm()` and PRINTS the skip. `Box[String].get()` is an `llc` hard
# error and `Box[bool].get()` through a plain parameter is rc 139 on LLVM — at
# pristine base AND under the fix — so the LLVM lane has nothing to assert here
# either way (`todo/t0685`, `todo/t1510`). Skipping a lane that cannot BUILD the
# program is not the same as excusing a lane that gets it wrong: the C-lane
# defect this pins is CLOSED, and without this file nothing in the tree holds it.
#
# ⚠ LIVES IN `tests/fixtures/self_host_gaps/`, NOT AT TOP LEVEL. Every top-level
# `tests/fixtures/*.gg` is auto-scanned into `runtime_parity_corpus`; the
# self-host lane has no `is_by_value_receiver` chokepoint to mirror this fix into
# (`todo/t1537`), and Core #9 ⊕ forbids raising `RUNTIME_DIFF_NONMATCH_CEILING`
# for a round's own inflow.

struct SS:
    Box[String] b

void main():
    Box[String] bb = Box("hi")
    SS s = SS(^bb)
    print(s.b.get())
